  "emoji": "📝",
  "summary": "Take the course's final exam: understand its four parts, its rules and the time allowed, talk about questions, answers and marks, say who passed (نَجَحَ) or failed (رَسَبَ), and congratulate with مَبْرُوك.",
  "intro": "Today is the day of the final exam, الِامْتِحَان النِّهَائِيّ. You will hear the words every student needs on exam day: question and answer (سُؤَال, إِجَابَة), mark (عَلَامَة), the time allowed (الْمُدَّة), to pass and to fail (نَجَحَ, رَسَبَ). The day's sentences sweep the whole course: greetings, numbers and time, past, present and future, comparatives like أَصْعَبَ, if-sentences with إِذَا, إِنْ and لَوْ, and the passive (تُكْتَبُ الْإِجَابَاتُ, the answers are written). Read them aloud with their case endings: -u for the subject, -a after kāna, inna and in objects, -i after a preposition. And when someone passes, say مَبْرُوك!",
